From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:55:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: preserve unaligned __bss head and tail bytes in DmShell
 segment snapshots

save_seg_snap() rounded the __bss scan start up to an 8-byte boundary and
advanced in 8-byte steps while restore_seg_snap() zeroed the entire [b0, b1)
range before restoring only 8-byte aligned slots, dropping 1..7 non-zero
initial bytes at an unaligned start, an unaligned end, or a sub-8-byte __bss
section when returning to the library.

Extract the segment snapshot helpers into dm/ios/Shell/SegSnap.h and
partition [b0, b1) without unsigned underflow or unaligned 64-bit pointer
casts into disjoint head bytes (0..7), 8-byte aligned interior words across
resident pages, and tail bytes (0..7). Restore both head and tail slices
alongside interior non-zero words after zeroing or anonymous page remapping.

Add C unit tests under ASan/UBSan in dm/host/tests/t_seg_snap.c covering
empty, sub-word, unaligned start/end, page-straddling and multi-page spans,
plus end-to-end Mach-O dylib tests in dm/ios/tests/test_seg_snap.py.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Preserve unaligned head and tail __bss bytes when resetting game framework segments in DmShell
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#451
